From: Gamejin <noreply@gamejin.local>
Subject: [PATCH] fake-08: preserve input edges between Lua updates

Fake-08's libretro host receives input every libretro frame, but a 30 FPS
PICO-8 cartridge runs its Lua input update only every other frame. Replacing
the current KDown state on each incoming frame lets a quick press-and-release
be overwritten before Host::scanInput() observes it.

Accumulate KDown bits in the libretro host and clear them only after
Host::scanInput() returns them to the VM. Held state remains a level value and
continues to be replaced every frame.

The cart runner already calls _update_buttons() before _update() or
_update60(). flip() calls _update_buttons() again before yielding, which
creates a second input sample in the same emulation cycle. Yield directly
after _draw() to preserve scheduling without the duplicate sample.

Fake-08 also implements PICO-8's btnp() hold-repeat behavior. Its repeat
interval was mistakenly read from btnpRepeatDelay, causing a custom interval
to be ignored. Read btnpRepeatInterval for the repeat cadence while continuing
to use btnpRepeatDelay for the initial delay.

---

diff --git a/source/Input.cpp b/source/Input.cpp
index c7e9c1e..dfefb2d 100644
--- a/source/Input.cpp
+++ b/source/Input.cpp
@@ -31,9 +31,9 @@ void Input::SetState(uint8_t kdown, uint8_t kheld){
         return;
     }
 
     uint8_t repeatInterval = _memory->hwState.btnpRepeatInterval == 0 
         ? 4 
-        : _memory->hwState.btnpRepeatDelay;
+        : _memory->hwState.btnpRepeatInterval;
 
     for (int i = 0; i < 7; i ++) {
         bool down = BITMASK(i) & kheld;

diff --git a/platform/libretro/libretrohost.cpp b/platform/libretro/libretrohost.cpp
--- a/platform/libretro/libretrohost.cpp
+++ b/platform/libretro/libretrohost.cpp
@@ -29,5 +29,7 @@ std::string _currentCartDirectory;
 void setInputState(uint8_t kDown, uint8_t kHeld, int16_t mouseX, int16_t mouseY, uint8_t mouseBtns) {
-    stubCurrKDown = kDown;
+    // A 30 FPS cart only samples input every other libretro frame.
+    // Retain press edges until Host::scanInput() consumes them.
+    stubCurrKDown |= kDown;
     stubCurrKHeld = kHeld;
     stubMouseX = mouseX;
     stubMouseY = mouseY;
@@ -68,3 +70,5 @@ InputState_t Host::scanInput(){
 InputState_t Host::scanInput(){
-    return InputState_t {stubCurrKDown, stubCurrKHeld, stubMouseX, stubMouseY, stubMouseBtns, stubCurrKBdown, stubCurrKBkey};
+    InputState_t input {stubCurrKDown, stubCurrKHeld, stubMouseX, stubMouseY, stubMouseBtns, stubCurrKBdown, stubCurrKBkey};
+    stubCurrKDown = 0;
+    return input;
 }
diff --git a/source/p8GlobalLuaFunctions.h b/source/p8GlobalLuaFunctions.h
--- a/source/p8GlobalLuaFunctions.h
+++ b/source/p8GlobalLuaFunctions.h
@@ -546,9 +546,9 @@ function __z8_run_cart(cart_code)
                     if (_update) _update()
                 end
                 if _draw then
                     _draw()
-                    flip()
+                    yield()
                 else
                     yield()
                 end
             end
